    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0220" n="132" xml:id="pg132"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-03-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 29,
                    1904</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Conger acknowledges receipt of Mr. Hay’s telegram of the 26th and states
                    that for the past two years a few Japanese officers have been employed with
                    Chines army as translators and instructors, and he has been reliably assured
                    that the number has not been increased recently and no new commands have been
                    given.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
